{% comment %}
  Testimonial card
  ----------------
  One review card. Rendered twice by the testimonials section:

    - mode: 'static'   — a card the merchant typed into a block, or a skeleton.
    - mode: 'template' — inside a <template>, with every hook emitted and left
                         empty. testimonials-judgeme.js clones it per review and
                         removes the hooks it has no data for.

  Because both paths come through here, a change to the markup lands on the
  Judge.me reviews and the hand-written ones at the same time.

  Accepts:
    mode          - 'static' (default) or 'template'
    block         - the section block, for theme-editor attributes
    rating        - 0-5
    title         - review headline
    body          - review text (richtext or string)
    author        - reviewer name
    location      - reviewer location
    date          - display date
    date_iso      - machine-readable date for <time datetime>
    product_title - product the review is about
    product_url   - link to that product
    verified      - truthy for the verified-buyer badge
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign is_template = false
  if mode == 'template'
    assign is_template = true
  endif

  assign show_stars = false
  if is_template
    assign show_stars = true
  elsif s.show_card_stars and rating > 0
    assign show_stars = true
  endif

  assign show_title = false
  if is_template
    assign show_title = true
  elsif s.show_card_title and title != blank
    assign show_title = true
  endif

  assign show_verified = false
  if is_template
    assign show_verified = true
  elsif s.show_verified and verified
    assign show_verified = true
  endif

  assign show_date = false
  if is_template
    assign show_date = true
  elsif s.show_date and date != blank
    assign show_date = true
  endif

  assign show_product = false
  if is_template
    assign show_product = true
  elsif s.show_product and product_title != blank
    assign show_product = true
  endif

  assign show_location = false
  if is_template
    assign show_location = true
  elsif location != blank
    assign show_location = true
  endif

  assign star_rating = rating
  if star_rating == blank or star_rating == 0
    assign star_rating = 5
  endif

  assign body_class = 'jm-review__body'
  if s.clamp_body
    assign body_class = 'jm-review__body jm-review__body--clamped'
  endif
-%}

<div class="jm-slider__slide"{% if block %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}{% endif %}>
  <figure class="jm-review">
    {%- comment -%}
      Drawn, not typed. A text quote mark drags along its font's full line box
      and em advance, so it reserved far more space than the mark itself
      occupied — and no line-height could take that back.

      Icon: "quote-left" from Font Awesome Free 7.3.1, CC BY 4.0
      (https://fontawesome.com, https://fontawesome.com/license/free),
      Copyright Fonticons, Inc.

      The viewBox is tightened to the path's own bounding box. Font Awesome
      ships it centred in a 640x640 square that is 65% empty, which would have
      reintroduced exactly the padding this SVG replaced.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if s.show_quote_mark and s.quote_mark_image != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        A merchant-supplied mark. The wrapper carries the size and is marked
        decorative, so a filename never reaches a screen reader whatever alt
        text the image was uploaded with. The mark tops out at 12rem, so 360w
        covers it on a 3x screen.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- capture quote_sizes -%}{{ s.quote_mark_size | times: 10 | round }}px{%- endcapture -%}
      <span class="jm-review__quote-mark" aria-hidden="true">
        {{
          s.quote_mark_image
          | image_url: width: 360
          | image_tag:
            widths: '40, 80, 120, 180, 240, 360',
            sizes: quote_sizes,
            class: 'jm-review__quote-image',
            alt: ''
        }}
      </span>
    {%- elsif s.show_quote_mark -%}
      <svg
        class="jm-review__quote-mark"
        viewBox="96 160 448 320"
        fill="currentColor"
        aria-hidden="true"
        focusable="false"
      >
        <path d="M96 280C96 213.7 149.7 160 216 160L224 160C241.7 160 256 174.3 256 192C256 209.7 241.7 224 224 224L216 224C185.1 224 160 249.1 160 280L160 288L224 288C259.3 288 288 316.7 288 352L288 416C288 451.3 259.3 480 224 480L160 480C124.7 480 96 451.3 96 416L96 280zM352 280C352 213.7 405.7 160 472 160L480 160C497.7 160 512 174.3 512 192C512 209.7 497.7 224 480 224L472 224C441.1 224 416 249.1 416 280L416 288L480 288C515.3 288 544 316.7 544 352L544 416C544 451.3 515.3 480 480 480L416 480C380.7 480 352 451.3 352 416L352 280z"/>
      </svg>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if show_stars -%}
      <span
        class="jm-review__stars jm-testimonials__stars"
        style="--jm-star-rating: {{ star_rating }};"
        role="img"
        aria-label="{{ star_rating }} out of 5 stars"
        data-jm-card-stars
      ></span>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if show_title -%}
      <p class="jm-review__title" data-jm-title>{{ title }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <blockquote class="{{ body_class }}" data-jm-body>{{ body }}</blockquote>

    <figcaption class="jm-review__footer">
      <div class="jm-review__meta">
        {%- if s.show_author -%}
          <p class="jm-review__author" data-jm-author>{{ author }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <span class="jm-review__sub" data-jm-sub>
          {%- if show_verified -%}
            <span class="jm-review__verified" data-jm-verified>
              <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <circle cx="8" cy="8" r="8" fill="currentColor" />
                <path
                  d="M4.6 8.3l2.1 2.1 4.7-4.7"
                  stroke="var(--jm-card-background, #fff)"
                  stroke-width="1.6"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                  stroke-linejoin="round"
                />
              </svg>
              {{ s.verified_label }}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if show_location -%}
            <span data-jm-location>{{ location }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if show_product -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              No href rather than href="#" when the product link is missing —
              a Judge.me shop review has no product to point at. The JS fills
              the href in when the review does carry one.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <a
              class="jm-review__product"
              {%- if product_url != blank %} href="{{ product_url }}"{% endif %}
              data-jm-product
            >{{ product_title }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if show_date -%}
            <time class="jm-review__date" datetime="{{ date_iso }}" data-jm-date>{{ date }}</time>
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
      </div>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</div>
